  "blockers": [
    "Full Node shell matrices on main and current candidates are 43/44: the sole failure is the T-20-owned Windows execution of the macOS Desktop artifact-path assertion; no WSL/container runner is available.",
    "G7 requires a real macOS Tauri/Keychain/native-window environment; the current Windows host cannot provide or substitute that required proof."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "DEV-10-001 (ticket path ownership, approved under USER-DECISION:all-approved): T-10 may update the existing Desktop product composition/private-route files, production App.vue, Rust proxy, Tauri app manifest/capability allowlist, and autogenerated setup command permissions. The setup transport must remain behind the loopback control-token boundary; password and raw Session/CSRF material may exist only transiently in the native command path and Rust vault, while WebView receives only setup state, a validated public profile, and completion/recovery signals. No public HTTP bootstrap endpoint or client-persisted setup flag is permitted.",
    "DEV-13-001 (ticket path ownership, approved under USER-DECISION:all-approved): T-13 may add dedicated desktop_session_heartbeat and desktop_session_renew commands in the minimal Rust proxy/main, Tauri app manifest, capability allowlist, and autogenerated command permissions. Rust must consume and commit cookie/CSRF rotation inside the native vault and return only a validated PublicProfile; generic desktop_request remains forbidden for Session maintenance.",
    "DEV-12-001 (ticket path ownership, approved under USER-DECISION:all-approved): T-12 may migrate exactly the Files Platform Port assertion in tests/shell/workspace-boundary.test.mjs from the removed static FilesPage composition to the compiled manifest loader and route-derived component props; adapter dependency and Desktop command allowlists remain unchanged.",
    "DEV-09-002 (ticket path ownership, approved under USER-DECISION:all-approved): T-09 may remove legacy cmd/migrate and cmd/config-check references from the canonical architecture list, command-boundary test, and existing CI/CodeQL build lists only; T-17 architecture evolution and T-18 required CI/security behavior remain unchanged.",
    "DEV-09-001 (ticket+release sequencing, approved by user 2026-08-31T22:50:26+08:00): Lead may build one audited Wave A backend candidate from reviewed T-01/T-02/T-03/T-04/T-06/T-07 sources and T-09 owner may provide an early migration/provider composition checkpoint. Wave A promotion uses the approved changed-scope/race/real-PG/vet/architecture/vulnerability gate plus an executed main-vs-candidate full-suite attribution; only identical Windows baseline failures and T-08-owned old rotate-on-read HTTP assertions may carry. T-09 closure dependencies and T-18~21 required gates remain unchanged.",
    "DEV-03-001 (ticket path + release sequencing, approved under USER-DECISION:2026-08-31-all-approved): T-03 may update exactly two Audit disposable fixtures to compose its 0040 provider; two Authorization fixtures remain with T-04 owner via composition checkpoint c35237ca60a1f99518a65fe03bfcc2d62b591cc4; production fallback and old rotate-on-read behavior remain prohibited."
  ],
